{:id "0009-rules"
 :title "Firestore rules for members, conversations, messages and presence, tested on the emulator in the gate"
 :lupa/area :security
 :lupa/risk :high
 :goal "Signed-in members can read the conversations they belong to and
        write their own messages and presence, and nobody else can read or
        write anything. The rules are tested against the Firestore emulator
        as part of `bb test`, on a free port so parallel factory worktrees
        never collide."
 :scope ["firestore.rules" "bb.edn" "src/halfahead/dev/emulator.clj"
         "test-rules/halfahead/rules_test.clj"]
 :design "firestore.rules (rules_version 2), deny by default:
          - members/{memberId}: read if signed in and a members document
            exists for request.auth.uid. No client writes.
          - conversations/{cid}: read if request.auth.uid is in
            resource.data.memberIds. No client writes.
          - conversations/{cid}/messages/{mid}: read if the uid is in the
            parent conversation's memberIds (get()). create only if: the uid
            is in memberIds; request.resource.data.authorId ==
            request.auth.uid; request.resource.data.id == mid;
            request.resource.data.conversationId == cid;
            request.resource.data.sentAt == request.time; keys().hasOnly the
            message wire keys (id, conversationId, authorId, text, delivery,
            emphasis, sentAt, inReplyTo); text is a string of size 1..4000;
            delivery is one of plain typed headline aside credits; emphasis
            is a list of size <= 8. No update or delete.
          - conversations/{cid}/presence/{memberId}: read if a member of the
            conversation; write only if memberId == request.auth.uid and the
            uid is a member.
          The worker writes through the emulator's admin bypass, so agent
          messages and presence are not constrained here (a later order
          gives agents real credentials).

          Tests: Babashka, over the Firestore REST API, in
          test-rules/halfahead/rules_test.clj (a separate root, so the
          offline runner never picks them up). Seed fixtures with the admin
          header \"Authorization: Bearer owner\"; act as a user with an
          unsigned emulator ID token (JWT with header {\"alg\":\"none\"}, an
          empty signature, and claims sub/user_id = uid, aud and iss for
          project demo-halfahead, iat/exp/auth_time, and
          firebase.sign_in_provider \"password\"). Read the emulator host
          from FIRESTORE_EMULATOR_HOST, which `firebase emulators:exec` sets.

          halfahead.dev.emulator (Babashka): (run-rules-tests!) finds a free
          TCP port for each emulator listener, writes a temporary firebase
          config (a copy of firebase.json whose firestore emulator port is a
          free port, with \"hub\" and \"logging\" also on free ports and
          \"ui\" disabled, because those default to fixed ports 4400 and
          4500 and collide across parallel runs; the rules path absolute),
          and runs
          `npx firebase emulators:exec --only firestore --project
          demo-halfahead --config <tmp> \"bb test:rules\"`, exiting non-zero
          when the tests fail.

          bb.edn: `test:rules` runs clojure.test over the test-rules
          namespaces (requires FIRESTORE_EMULATOR_HOST); `test` gains a
          final step calling halfahead.dev.emulator/run-rules-tests!; add
          \"test-rules\" to :paths. Keep every existing task working."
 :acceptance
 ["Allowed: a member reads their conversation, its messages, and members;
   a member creates a valid message as themselves with sentAt =
   request.time (use the REST serverValue transform REQUEST_TIME); a member
   writes their own presence"
  "Denied: a non-member reads the conversation or its messages; a signed-out
   request reads anything; a member creates a message with another
   authorId, an extra key, blank text, an unknown delivery, or a client
   sentAt; a member updates or deletes a message; a member writes another
   member's presence; any client writes members or conversations"
  "Two `bb test` runs at once (from two directories) both pass: the port is
   chosen per run (assert in a unit test of the free-port and config
   functions, which are pure or nearly so)"
  "`bb test` runs the offline suites, then the rules suite, and fails if
   any fails"]
 :non-goals
 ["Do not edit src/halfahead (except the new dev/emulator.clj), the
   schema, or firebase.json"
  "No Storage rules; no auth providers; no client code"]
 :context ["DESIGN.md" "docs/SCHEMA.md" "src/halfahead/codec.cljc"
           "src/halfahead/worker/store.clj" "firebase.json" "firestore.rules"
           "bb.edn"]
 :budget-usd 12.0}
